+rendering invalidation, terminal visual selection, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends
+chat text to the selected agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is
+selected. Bracketed-paste newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits
+the buffered chat text. When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds
+the chat buffer with `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the
+selected-agent backend command path.
+
+Terminal visual selection is local UI state owned by `TerminalUi`. In command mode, `v`, `V`, and
+`Ctrl-V` start character, line, and block selection in the focused pane. Vim-style movement keys and
+terminal arrow escape sequences extend the selection, `y` yanks the selected range, `Y` yanks whole
+lines, and the rendered frame emits an OSC 52 clipboard sequence for the yank buffer.
 
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
